.TH VYT 1 "2026" "vyt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vyt \- a tiny C wrapper around yt-dlp and mpv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vyt
.B \-m
.I URL
.br
.B vyt
.B \-v
.I URL
.br
.B vyt
.B \-s
.I QUERY
.br
.B vyt
.B playlist
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B vyt
.B \-V
.br
.B vyt
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vyt
is a tiny wrapper around
.BR yt-dlp (1)
and
.BR mpv (1)
that lets you play or search YouTube content with short,
memorable commands instead of typing out long
.B mpv
or
.B yt-dlp
invocations.
.PP
In addition to single-URL playback and search,
.B vyt
manages persistent named playlists stored as plain text files on disk.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " URL"
Play
.I URL
as music: audio only, via
.BR "mpv --no-video" .
.TP
.BI \-v " URL"
Play
.I URL
as video, via
.BR mpv .
.TP
.BI \-s " QUERY"
Search YouTube for
.I QUERY
via
.BR yt-dlp ,
printing the top 10 results as "title | URL".
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage and exit.
.SH PLAYLISTS
.B vyt
stores playlists as plain text files under the playlists directory (see
.B FILES
below). Each playlist is one file, each song is one line, and songs must
be
.B http://
or
.B https://
URLs. The directory is created on first use.
.SS Playlist commands
.TP
.BI "vyt playlist add " name
Create a new, empty playlist called
.IR name .
Fails if a playlist with that name already exists.
.TP
.B "vyt playlist list"
Print the name of every playlist, sorted alphabetically.
An empty playlists directory is not an error.
.TP
.BI "vyt playlist remove " name
Delete the playlist called
.IR name .
The file is removed; songs are not recoverable.
.TP
.BI "vyt playlist song add " "name url"
Append
.I url
to playlist
.IR name .
Duplicates are rejected.
Both
.I name
and
.I url
are validated; see
.B FILES
for the file naming rules.
.TP
.BI "vyt playlist song remove " "name url"
Remove the first occurrence of
.I url
from playlist
.IR name .
It is not an error if the URL appears more than once; only the first
match is removed.
.TP
.BI "vyt playlist song list " name
Print every URL in playlist
.IR name ,
one per line, in the order they were added.
.TP
.BI "vyt playlist play " name
Play playlist
.I name
in random order, using
.B "mpv --no-video"
(the same path as
.BR "vyt \-m" ).
When more than one song is present,
.B vyt
never picks the same song twice in a row.
Playback continues indefinitely until interrupted; see
.B SIGNALS
below.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vyt/playlists/
Default location for playlist files. Created on first use with
.B "mkdir \-p"
semantics.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vyt/playlists/
Used instead of the default if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set and absolute.
.TP
Playlist names may be at most 64 bytes, must not contain
.BR / ,
control characters, leading or trailing whitespace, or be
.B .
or
.BR .. .
A playlist name becomes a filename, so these rules keep it inside the
playlists directory.
.TP
Writes are atomic: a new playlist is written to a hidden temporary file
in the same directory,
.BR fsync (2)ed,
and
.BR rename (2)ed
over the original.
An interrupted
.B vyt
can never leave a half-written playlist file.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT
During
.BR "vyt playlist play" ,
Ctrl+C stops playback cleanly:
.B vyt
finishes waiting for the currently running
.B mpv
child to exit, prints
.RB ` "vyt: stopped." ',
and exits with status 0.
The signal handler is installed only for the duration of the
.B play
command and restored afterwards.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Treated identically to
.B SIGINT
during playback.
.SH EXIT STATUS
If
.B vyt
launches
.B mpv
or
.BR yt-dlp ,
its exit status is that of the underlying process.
.PP
For playlist commands,
.B vyt
exits 0 on success and 1 on any error (missing playlist, duplicate URL,
invalid name, filesystem failure, etc.).
.PP
Stopping playback with Ctrl+C is considered normal termination, not an
error: the exit status is 0.
.PP
Non-zero if
.B vyt
itself failed to parse arguments or launch the process.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B yt-dlp
and
.B mpv
must be installed and available on
.BR PATH .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp (1),
.BR mpv (1)
